these days you can 3d print plastic at  the local copy store plastics are easy  to process they are flexible and melts  at relatively low temperatures but  plastics are much weaker materials when  compared to metals or ceramics ceramics  have a lot of desirable properties  they're highly heat resistant and strong  for example they've been used to shield  shuttles during reentry  however being heat resistant and brittle  means it's not easy to make ceramics  into complex shapes it also makes it  hard to 3d print them enter polymer  derived ceramics these materials start  out as a polymer and through a heating  process are converted into a ceramic now  we are set for 3d printing first the  polymer is shot with a laser this UV  light causes polymerization  wherever the mask is not present giving  the emerging solid a complex shape then  the printed polymer is baked at 1,000  degrees while exposed to argon gas these  3d printed ceramics have 10 times the  compressive strength of commercially  available materials and survive  temperatures up to 1700 degrees Celsius
 

